Program Bug_2_20_PathtoolDesync;
// Bug 2.20: `@pathtool` never compiles, in any configuration. This
// compiler parses the whole file more than once across different phases.
// On an early phase, `@pathtool` runs through the normal preprocessor
// dispatch table and its handler correctly consumes all five of its
// tokens (directive name, two string args, two integer args), running
// its real side effects (reading the input file, fitting the curve,
// writing the three output .bin files) in the process. On the later
// code-generation phase, the same directive is instead reached through a
// separate "skip already-executed directives" table, whose `pathtool`
// entry only consumes four tokens - one integer short of what the
// directive actually has. The trailing `degreeSteps` integer is left in
// the token stream, desyncing everything parsed afterward (same dropped-
// token shape as 2.8/2.12). `@perlinnoise`'s equivalent skip-table entry
// correctly consumes all of its tokens, which is why it doesn't fail the
// same way.
//
// Method B (compile-time desync), no VICE step. Confirmed live: this
// fails with "After declarations, BEGIN is expected", a confusing error
// that doesn't point at the `@pathtool` line itself. The directive's own
// side effects DO run first: 2_20_pathtool_desync_out_x.bin/_y.bin/_t.bin
// are written to this directory before the error surfaces (confirmed by
// checking the files exist with the expected size after a compile
// attempt). Pre-fix expected behavior: compile failure with that error.
// Post-fix, once the code-generation-phase skip-table entry for
// `pathtool` consumes all five tokens like its real handler does, this
// should compile clean.
//
// 2_20_pathtool_input.svg is a minimal path-tool input: despite the .svg
// extension, Tool::PathTool doesn't parse real SVG/XML, it just reads
// whitespace-simplified "x,y ..." triples (only the first token of every
// 3 is actually used as a coordinate pair) and fits a degree-4 spline
// through them.

var

@pathtool "2_20_pathtool_input.svg" "2_20_pathtool_desync_out_" 4 8

	dummy : byte;

begin
	loop();
end.
